#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:71
msgid "A single run produces the following layout under `TL_LOWER_TRACE_DIR`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:73
msgid ""
"<TL_LOWER_TRACE_DIR>/\n"
"└── <script_name>/                      # derived from sys.argv[0], e.g. "
"\"my_script\"\n"
"    ├── report.html                     # symlink → latest run's report\n"
"    ├── codegen_device.cpp              # generated device source (editable, "
"see below)\n"
"    ├── codegen_device.cpp.original     # device baseline for edit/recompile "
"workflow\n"
"    ├── codegen_device.cpp.latest       # latest generated device source\n"
"    ├── codegen_host.cpp                # generated CPU wrapper, when host "
"codegen runs\n"
"    ├── codegen_host.cpp.original       # independent host baseline\n"
"    ├── codegen_host.cpp.latest         # latest generated host source\n"
"    └── .run_records/\n"
"        └── run_<YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_ffffff>_<pid>_<unique-id>/\n"
"            ├── report.html             # this run's full report\n"
"            ├── pipeline_c/             # one subdir per phase (example)\n"
"            │   ├── 00_BindTarget_before.tir\n"
"            │   ├── 00_BindTarget_after.tir\n"
"            │   ├── 01_Simplify_before.tir\n"
"            │   └── 01_Simplify_after.tir\n"
"            ├── phase2_optimize/        # another phase (illustrative)\n"
"            │   └── ...\n"
"            ├── codegen/\n"
"            │   ├── 42_codegen_device_before.tir\n"
"            │   ├── 42_codegen_device_after.cpp\n"
"            │   ├── 49_codegen_host_before.tir\n"
"            │   └── 49_codegen_host_after.cpp\n"
"            └── unscoped/               # passes outside any pipeline "
"window\n"
"                └── ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:102
msgid ""
"Each phase gets its own subdirectory; passes are numbered globally (`00_`, "
"`01_`, …) so ordering is unambiguous. Codegen records write the *after* "
"artifact as `.cpp` (the generated source), while ordinary passes use `.tir` "
"for both sides. Both device and host records belong to the `codegen` phase, "
"with names `codegen_device` and `codegen_host` respectively. Host files and "
"records appear only when the execution backend invokes host codegen. Each "
"working file has its own baseline, latest output, and backups; host codegen "
"cannot overwrite the device working file or its editing state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:111
msgid ""
"The standard backend wrappers explicitly identify each event as device or "
"host codegen. Generic instrumentation calls that omit `role` leave it "
"unspecified (`None`): these retain the `codegen` record name and default "
"`codegen.cpp` working file. An explicit `codegen_output` path is used "
"unchanged for such events. Custom callers should supply a role to "
"distinguish device and host output; unspecified events share the legacy "
"working file and edit state."
msgstr ""

