msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:0
msgid "`codegen_output`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:0
msgid ""
"Device working-file path; a host working-file path is derived when host "
"codegen runs. Pass `None` explicitly to suppress both working files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:0
msgid ""
"`<script_dir>/codegen_device.cpp` and `<script_dir>/codegen_host.cpp` in "
"`html`/`both` mode; no working files in `terminal` mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:184
msgid ""
"An explicit `codegen_output=\"foo.cpp\"` writes device source to `foo.cpp` "
"and host source to `foo_host.cpp`. The host path inserts `_host` before the "
"final extension: `foo.kernel.cpp` becomes `foo.kernel_host.cpp`, and a path "
"without an extension, such as `foo`, becomes `foo_host`. Each path has its "
"own `.original`, `.latest`, and backup files. Setting `codegen_output=None` "
"suppresses these stable working files and their edit state, while codegen "
"records still appear in the trace and raw snapshots remain available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:192
msgid ""
"`enable()` is idempotent — calling it multiple times is safe. Its values are "
"snapshotted when a compilation begins, so changing them cannot mutate a "
"kernel that is already compiling."
msgstr ""

