#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:250
msgid "Codegen Source Capture & Edit-Recompile Workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:252
msgid ""
"When tracing is enabled, device and host codegen steps (TIR → C/CUDA/HIP/…) "
"are intercepted separately. Device source runs on the GPU or NPU and "
"contains the computation, device memory transfers, and synchronization. Host "
"source runs on the CPU and wraps runtime operations such as argument checks, "
"output allocation, and launching the device kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/lower_trace.md:258
msgid ""
"In `html`/`both` mode, the generated sources are written to `<script_dir>/"
"codegen_device.cpp` and `<script_dir>/codegen_host.cpp` by default. For CUDA "
"and Ascend, `tvm_ffi` invokes both device and host codegen; `nvrtc` and "
"`cython` do not invoke a separate host codegen step at this layer. Their "
"runtime adapters still provide CPU-side launch logic. Only backends that "
"invoke host codegen produce `codegen_host.cpp`."
msgstr ""

